      "message": "During reload, the `onReloadPlugin(oldPlugin, newPlugin)` replaces the filter registrations before `unloadPlugin(oldPlugin)` invokes `beforeStopPlugin()`.\n\n1. The replacement plugin starts: [PluginLoader.java:524](https://github.com/GerritCodeReview/gerrit/blob/9f270d273e4baaadfc8f55c31489d99d1d0da65f/java/com/google/gerrit/server/plugins/PluginLoader.java#L524)\n2. It replacas the registrations: [PluginLoader.java:531](https://github.com/GerritCodeReview/gerrit/blob/9f270d273e4baaadfc8f55c31489d99d1d0da65f/java/com/google/gerrit/server/plugins/PluginLoader.java#L531)\n\nOnly then is the old plugin unloaded:\n\n3. Unload the old plugin: [PluginLoader.java:532](https://github.com/GerritCodeReview/gerrit/blob/9f270d273e4baaadfc8f55c31489d99d1d0da65f/java/com/google/gerrit/server/plugins/PluginLoader.java#L532)\n\nSo at this point, looking up filters by plugin name selects the _replacement_ instance\u0027s filters.\nWouldn’t this destroy the _new_ filters instead of the _old_ ones?\n\nI think the old cleanup was looking at previously initialised filters and destroying those no longer present in the shared set.",
